From: DshanPi Mainline Team <mainline@dshanpi.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mtd: spinand: gate DshanPi legacy EE OOB migration

Legacy DshanPi images filled the free OOB bytes of alternating W25N02KV
eraseblocks with 0xee.  Allow only an explicitly marked installer device
tree to treat the exact EE EE marker as erasable.  Keep every other non-FF
marker protected as a bad block.

---
 drivers/mtd/nand/spi/core.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/core.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/nand/spi/core.c
@@ -990,6 +990,23 @@ static bool spinand_isbad(struct nand_device *nand, const struct nand_pos *pos)
 		spinand_read_page(spinand, &req);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The legacy DshanPi image stored 0xee in the complete free OOB area
+	 * of alternating W25N02KV eraseblocks.  That pattern is payload
+	 * metadata, not a factory bad-block marker.  Permit a dedicated
+	 * installer DT to erase those blocks while preserving every other
+	 * non-0xff marker as bad.
+	 */
+	if (marker[0] == 0xee && marker[1] == 0xee &&
+	    spinand->id.len >= 3 && spinand->id.data[0] == 0xef &&
+	    spinand->id.data[1] == 0xaa && spinand->id.data[2] == 0x22 &&
+	    device_property_read_bool(&spinand->spimem->spi->dev,
+				      "dshanpi,legacy-ee-bbm")) {
+		dev_warn_once(&spinand->spimem->spi->dev,
+			      "treating legacy 0xee OOB metadata as erasable\n");
+		return false;
+	}
+
 	if (marker[0] != 0xff || marker[1] != 0xff)
 		return true;
 
-- 
